-- what this platform can build --
  cortado has this many kinds: 29
  every one of them answers yes or no: true
  a control is alive exactly where the kind is offered: true
  and refused before it is built exactly where it is not: true
  every refusal names the control rather than a handle: true
-- what a control that exists can say about itself --
  each has an accessibility role, and none is empty: true
  each has the platform's own class name, and none is empty: true
-- the same question through markup --
  this many kinds are reachable by their own name as a tag: 28
  and each builds exactly where its kind is offered: true
-- moving a control, and writing to one --
  this many kinds are a state: 3
  each one this platform has raises value_changed when it is moved: true
  and none raises anything when the program writes to it: true
-- what can be turning --
  exactly a spinner, and only where there is one: true
-- a number that is not a kind --
  the host refuses it rather than calling it a missing control: true
  and cortado has no name for it: true
drove=true
